          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why is osteoarthritis not simply “wear and tear” of a joint?",
          "answer": "Osteoarthritis is much more than just \"wear and tear\" on a joint. It is a complex disorder affecting the entire joint, including the cartilage, bone, ligaments, joint lining, and surrounding muscles. Characterizing it simply as wear and tear can be misleading and may lead to incorrect responses, such as excessive rest, which can actually worsen the condition. \n\nThe process of osteoarthritis involves active inflammation and an attempt by the body to repair the damaged joint structures, rather than just mechanical erosion. For instance, when cartilage begins to degrade, the underlying bone can change in response, leading to further complications. Additionally, muscle weakness from reduced use can exacerbate joint problems, making exercise an essential part of management rather than a mere adjunct to treatment (source: General clinical reference on Osteoarthritis).\n\nUnderstanding these complexities allows for a more comprehensive approach to treatment, focused on maintaining joint function and quality of life rather than just addressing symptoms.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
